---
import AdSlot from '../../components/AdSlot.astro';
import EntryChecker from '../../components/EntryChecker.astro';
import RelatedPosts from '../../components/RelatedPosts.astro';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Korea Entry Requirements Check: Visa-Free, K-ETA, e-Arrival Card"
  description="Three questions people arrive believing are one. Check whether your passport is in scope for visa-free entry and for how long, whether K-ETA applies, and whether you file the e-Arrival Card — each answered separately, each citing the official page it came from."
>
  <header class="mb-8">
    <h1 class="mb-3 font-display text-4xl font-bold text-ink">
      Korea entry requirements check
    </h1>
    <p class="mb-3 max-w-2xl text-slate-600">
      Visa-free entry, K-ETA and the e-Arrival Card are three separate
      decisions, and most of the confusion comes from treating them as one. The
      sharpest example: being exempt from K-ETA does not exempt you from the
      arrival declaration — it puts you on the list of people who file it.
    </p>
    <p class="max-w-2xl text-slate-600">
      Nothing here is a promise of admission. An immigration officer decides
      that at the counter, and every answer below links the official page it was
      read from so you can check it yourself.
    </p>
  </header>

  <EntryChecker />

  <AdSlot position="bottom" />

  <RelatedPosts category="employment" heading="Before you arrive" />
</Layout>
